# `a&&b` without spaces: the fix adds them.
mode: syntax
---- query
'orders.csv' | where a&&b
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..26
  PIPELINE@0..25
    LITERAL@0..12
      STRING@0..12 "'orders.csv'"
    WHITESPACE@12..13 " "
    PIPE@13..14 "|"
    WHITESPACE@14..15 " "
    WHERE_OP@15..25
      IDENT@15..20 "where"
      WHITESPACE@20..21 " "
      BIN_EXPR@21..25
        NAME_REF@21..22
          IDENT@21..22 "a"
        AMP2@22..24 "&&"
        NAME_REF@24..25
          IDENT@24..25 "b"
  WHITESPACE@25..26 "\n"

error[DS0111]: `&&` is not an operator
  --> query:1:23
  |
1 | 'orders.csv' | where a&&b
  |                       ^^
  |
  = help: use `and` to require both conditions: `a and b`

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    'orders.csv' | where a and b
which parses without errors
